{
  "name": "clojure-pulse",
  "displayName": "Clojure Pulse",
  "description": "Lightweight, powerful Clojure and let-go support, powered by the clj-pulse language server.",
  "version": "0.2.0",
  "publisher": "abogoyavlensky",
  "license": "MIT",
  "author": "Andrey Bogoyavlenskiy",
  "icon": "images/icon.png",
  "repository": {
    "type": "git",
    "url": "https://github.com/abogoyavlensky/clojure-pulse-vscode"
  },
  "engines": {
    "vscode": "^1.85.0"
  },
  "categories": [
    "Programming Languages",
    "Linters"
  ],
  "main": "./dist/extension.js",
  "activationEvents": [
    "onLanguage:clojure",
    "workspaceContains:**/deps.edn",
    "workspaceContains:**/project.clj",
    "workspaceContains:**/lgx.edn"
  ],
  "contributes": {
    "languages": [
      {
        "id": "clojure",
        "aliases": [
          "Clojure",
          "clojure"
        ],
        "extensions": [
          ".clj",
          ".cljs",
          ".cljc",
          ".edn",
          ".bb",
          ".lg"
        ],
        "configuration": "./language-configuration.json"
      }
    ],
    "grammars": [
      {
        "language": "clojure",
        "scopeName": "source.clojure",
        "path": "./syntaxes/clojure.tmLanguage.json"
      }
    ],
    "configuration": {
      "title": "Clojure Pulse",
      "properties": {
        "clojurePulse.server.path": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "clj-pulse",
          "markdownDescription": "Path to the `clj-pulse` language server binary. A bare name (e.g. `clj-pulse`) is resolved from your `PATH`; an absolute or relative path is used as-is."
        },
        "clojurePulse.server.args": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "default": [],
          "description": "Extra command-line arguments passed to the clj-pulse server on startup."
        },
        "clojurePulse.trace.server": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "off",
            "messages",
            "verbose"
          ],
          "default": "off",
          "description": "Traces the communication between VS Code and the clj-pulse language server."
        },
        "clojurePulse.maintainIndentation": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "markdownDescription": "Keep relative indentation while editing (Cursive-style): when an edit moves code that later lines of a multiline form are anchored to — spaces before an opening bracket, a newline inserted before a form, a head symbol like `->` renamed to `cond->` — those lines shift by the same amount automatically. Disable this if you use Parinfer's Smart Mode, which does the same job."
        },
        "clojurePulse.dimIgnoredForms": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "markdownDescription": "Dim `#_` discard forms and `(comment …)` blocks (brackets included). Reload the window to toggle."
        },
        "clojurePulse.dimIgnoredFormsOpacity": {
          "type": "number",
          "default": 0.6,
          "minimum": 0.1,
          "maximum": 1,
          "markdownDescription": "Opacity for dimmed `#_`/`(comment …)` forms — lower is more faded. Reload the window to apply."
        },
        "clojurePulse.inlineEvalResults": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "markdownDescription": "Show evaluation results inline in the editor as ghost text (` => value`) at the end of the evaluated form. Hover the result for the full value and a Copy link. When off, results appear only in the REPL's output channel (`REPL: <name>` in the Output panel)."
        },
        "clojurePulse.replConfigurations": {
          "type": "array",
          "default": [],
          "scope": "resource",
          "markdownDescription": "Named REPLs shown in the **REPL** view. Each entry either starts a server (`\"type\": \"create\"`) or attaches to a running one (`\"type\": \"connect\"`).\n\n```json\n[\n  { \"name\": \"dev\", \"type\": \"create\",\n    \"command\": \"clojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:clojure-pulse/nrepl {:extra-deps {nrepl/nrepl {:mvn/version \\\"1.7.0\\\"}} :main-opts [\\\"-m\\\" \\\"nrepl.cmdline\\\"]}}}' -M:clojure-pulse/nrepl\" },\n  { \"name\": \"local\", \"type\": \"connect\", \"port\": \".nrepl-port\" }\n]\n```\n\nAdd your own aliases by editing the command — `-M:dev:test:clojure-pulse/nrepl` merges their `:extra-deps` and still starts nREPL.",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "name",
              "type"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "name": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Unique name, shown in the REPL view. Also the name of its output channel (REPL: <name>)."
              },
              "type": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "create",
                  "connect"
                ],
                "enumDescriptions": [
                  "Start an nREPL server with the given command, then connect to it.",
                  "Connect to an nREPL server that is already running."
                ]
              },
              "command": {
                "type": "string",
                "markdownDescription": "`create` only — the command line that starts the server, run through your shell. Required for `create`."
              },
              "cwd": {
                "type": "string",
                "default": ".",
                "markdownDescription": "`create` only — working directory for the command, relative to the workspace root."
              },
              "host": {
                "type": "string",
                "default": "localhost",
                "markdownDescription": "`connect` only — host of the running server."
              },
              "port": {
                "type": [
                  "number",
                  "string"
                ],
                "markdownDescription": "`connect` only — a port number, or a path to a file holding one (e.g. `\".nrepl-port\"`), relative to the workspace root. Required for `connect`."
              }
            },
            "additionalProperties": false
          },
          "defaultSnippets": [
            {
              "label": "create — start an nREPL server",
              "body": {
                "name": "$1dev",
                "type": "create",
                "command": "clojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:clojure-pulse/nrepl {:extra-deps {nrepl/nrepl {:mvn/version \"1.7.0\"}} :main-opts [\"-m\" \"nrepl.cmdline\"]}}}' -M:clojure-pulse/nrepl"
              }
            },
            {
              "label": "connect — attach to a running server",
              "body": {
                "name": "$1local",
                "type": "connect",
                "port": ".nrepl-port"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "clojurePulse.customReplCommands": {
          "type": "array",
          "default": [],
          "scope": "resource",
          "markdownDescription": "Named snippets of Clojure code shown in the **REPL Commands** view and run against the active REPL. Use fully-qualified symbols (e.g. `(user/reset)`). Bind one to a key by name:\n\n```json\n{ \"key\": \"ctrl+alt+r\", \"command\": \"clojurePulse.runCustomReplCommand\", \"args\": \"reset\" }\n```",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "name",
              "code"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "name": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Unique name, shown in the REPL Commands view and used as keybinding args."
              },
              "code": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Clojure code sent verbatim to the active REPL."
              }
            },
            "additionalProperties": false
          },
          "defaultSnippets": [
            {
              "label": "custom REPL command",
              "body": {
                "name": "$1reset",
                "code": "(user/reset)"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "clojurePulse.projects": {
          "type": "array",
          "default": [],
          "scope": "resource",
          "markdownDescription": "Per-project overrides for monorepo workspaces, shown in the **External Libraries** view. Paths are workspace-root-relative (`\".\"` is the root). Each entry overrides what the server auto-detected for that project — or adds a project detection missed (e.g. a subproject under a gitignored directory).\n\n```json\n[\n  { \"path\": \"apps/backend\",\n    \"classpathEnabled\": true,\n    \"classpathCommand\": \"clojure -A:dev:test -Spath\" }\n]\n```",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "path"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "path": {
                "type": "string",
                "markdownDescription": "Project directory, relative to the workspace root. `\".\"` is the root project."
              },
              "classpathEnabled": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "markdownDescription": "Whether the server resolves this project's full JVM classpath (running its classpath command) to index libraries."
              },
              "classpathCommand": {
                "type": "string",
                "markdownDescription": "Command that prints the project's classpath (e.g. `clojure -A:dev:test -Spath`), run in the project directory. Omit to use the server's default for the project's build tool."
              }
            },
            "additionalProperties": false
          },
          "defaultSnippets": [
            {
              "label": "project override",
              "body": {
                "path": "$1apps/backend",
                "classpathEnabled": true
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "configurationDefaults": {
      "[clojure]": {
        "editor.formatOnType": false
      }
    },
    "viewsContainers": {
      "activitybar": [
        {
          "id": "clojurePulseSidebar",
          "title": "Clojure Pulse",
          "icon": "images/activity-icon.svg"
        }
      ]
    },
    "views": {
      "clojurePulseSidebar": [
        {
          "id": "clojurePulse.replManager",
          "name": "REPL"
        },
        {
          "id": "clojurePulse.customCommands",
          "name": "REPL Commands"
        },
        {
          "id": "clojurePulse.externalLibraries",
          "name": "External Libraries"
        }
      ]
    },
    "viewsWelcome": [
      {
        "view": "clojurePulse.replManager",
        "contents": "No REPLs configured yet.\n\nAdd one to start an nREPL server for this project, or to connect to a server you already have running.\n\n[Add REPL Configuration](command:clojurePulse.addReplConfig)"
      },
      {
        "view": "clojurePulse.customCommands",
        "contents": "No commands yet.\n\nSave snippets like (user/reset) to run against the active REPL — from here, the palette, or your own keybindings.\n\n[Add Command](command:clojurePulse.addCustomReplCommand)"
      },
      {
        "view": "clojurePulse.externalLibraries",
        "contents": "No libraries resolved yet.\n\nThe clj-pulse language server lists the dependencies it resolved for this project here.\n\n- deps.edn: run `clojure -Spath` or start a REPL once to generate `.cpcache`.\n- Leiningen: direct dependencies only (best effort).\n- lgx: run `lgx run` or `lgx build` once to fetch deps."
      }
    ],
    "commands": [
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.restart",
        "title": "Restart Server",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.showOutput",
        "title": "Show Output",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.newline",
        "title": "Insert Newline and Indent",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.connectRepl",
        "title": "Connect to Running nREPL",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse",
        "icon": "$(plug)"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.disconnectRepl",
        "title": "Disconnect from nREPL",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.startRepl",
        "title": "Start REPL",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse",
        "icon": "$(play)"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.stopRepl",
        "title": "Stop REPL",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse",
        "icon": "$(debug-stop)"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.addReplConfig",
        "title": "Add REPL Configuration",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse",
        "icon": "$(add)"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.editReplConfig",
        "title": "Edit REPL Configuration",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse",
        "icon": "$(edit)"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.deleteReplConfig",
        "title": "Delete REPL Configuration",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse",
        "icon": "$(trash)"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.setActiveRepl",
        "title": "Set Active REPL",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse",
        "icon": "$(target)"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.showReplOutput",
        "title": "Show REPL Output",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse",
        "icon": "$(output)"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.evalSelection",
        "title": "Evaluate Selection",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.evalCurrentForm",
        "title": "Evaluate Current Form",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.evalFile",
        "title": "Evaluate File",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.runTestAtCursor",
        "title": "Run Test at Cursor",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.runNsTests",
        "title": "Run Tests in Namespace",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.rerunLastTest",
        "title": "Run Last Test Command",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.clearInlineResults",
        "title": "Clear Inline Results",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.copyEvalResult",
        "title": "Copy Evaluation Result",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.replMenu",
        "title": "REPL Menu",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.runCustomReplCommand",
        "title": "Run Custom REPL Command",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse",
        "icon": "$(play)"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.addCustomReplCommand",
        "title": "Add Custom REPL Command",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse",
        "icon": "$(add)"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.editCustomReplCommand",
        "title": "Edit Custom REPL Command",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse",
        "icon": "$(edit)"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.deleteCustomReplCommand",
        "title": "Delete Custom REPL Command",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse",
        "icon": "$(trash)"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.refreshExternalLibraries",
        "title": "Refresh External Libraries",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse",
        "icon": "$(refresh)"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.enableProjectClasspath",
        "title": "Enable Classpath Resolution",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse",
        "icon": "$(debug-start)"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.disableProjectClasspath",
        "title": "Disable Classpath Resolution",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse",
        "icon": "$(debug-stop)"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.addProject",
        "title": "Add Project",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse",
        "icon": "$(add)"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.editProject",
        "title": "Edit Project",
        "category": "Clojure Pulse",
        "icon": "$(edit)"
      }
    ],
    "menus": {
      "view/title": [
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.addReplConfig",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.replManager",
          "group": "navigation"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.addCustomReplCommand",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.customCommands",
          "group": "navigation"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.refreshExternalLibraries",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.externalLibraries",
          "group": "navigation"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.addProject",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.externalLibraries",
          "group": "navigation"
        }
      ],
      "view/item/context": [
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.startRepl",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.replManager && viewItem == replCreateStopped",
          "group": "inline@1"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.connectRepl",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.replManager && viewItem == replConnectStopped",
          "group": "inline@1"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.setActiveRepl",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.replManager && viewItem =~ /^(replCreateRunning|replConnectConnected)$/",
          "group": "inline@1"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.stopRepl",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.replManager && viewItem =~ /^(replCreateRunning|replConnectConnected)$/",
          "group": "inline@2"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.editReplConfig",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.replManager",
          "group": "inline@3"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.showReplOutput",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.replManager",
          "group": "1_output@1"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.editReplConfig",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.replManager",
          "group": "2_config@1"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.deleteReplConfig",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.replManager",
          "group": "2_config@2"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.runCustomReplCommand",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.customCommands && viewItem == customReplCommand",
          "group": "inline@1"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.editCustomReplCommand",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.customCommands && viewItem == customReplCommand",
          "group": "inline@2"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.runCustomReplCommand",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.customCommands && viewItem == customReplCommand",
          "group": "1_run@1"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.editCustomReplCommand",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.customCommands && viewItem == customReplCommand",
          "group": "2_config@1"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.deleteCustomReplCommand",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.customCommands && viewItem == customReplCommand",
          "group": "2_config@2"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.enableProjectClasspath",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.externalLibraries && viewItem == clojurePulseProjectDisabled",
          "group": "inline@1"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.disableProjectClasspath",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.externalLibraries && viewItem == clojurePulseProjectEnabled",
          "group": "inline@1"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.enableProjectClasspath",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.externalLibraries && viewItem == clojurePulseProjectDisabled",
          "group": "1_classpath@1"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.disableProjectClasspath",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.externalLibraries && viewItem == clojurePulseProjectEnabled",
          "group": "1_classpath@1"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.editProject",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.externalLibraries && viewItem =~ /^clojurePulseProject(Enabled|Disabled)$/",
          "group": "inline@2"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.editProject",
          "when": "view == clojurePulse.externalLibraries && viewItem =~ /^clojurePulseProject(Enabled|Disabled)$/",
          "group": "2_config@1"
        }
      ],
      "commandPalette": [
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.enableProjectClasspath",
          "when": "false"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.disableProjectClasspath",
          "when": "false"
        },
        {
          "command": "clojurePulse.editProject",
          "when": "false"
        }
      ]
    },
    "keybindings": [
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.newline",
        "key": "enter",
        "when": "editorTextFocus && !editorReadonly && editorLangId == clojure && !suggestWidgetVisible && !renameInputVisible && !inSnippetMode && !codeActionMenuVisible"
      },
      {
        "command": "clojurePulse.clearInlineResults",
        "key": "escape",
        "when": "editorTextFocus && editorLangId == clojure && clojurePulse.hasInlineResults && !suggestWidgetVisible && !renameInputVisible && !parameterHintsVisible && !findWidgetVisible && !inSnippetMode && !editorHasSelection"
      }
    ]
  },
  "scripts": {
    "compile": "tsc --noEmit && node esbuild.js",
    "watch": "node esbuild.js --watch",
    "package-build": "tsc --noEmit && node esbuild.js --production",
    "vscode:prepublish": "npm run package-build",
    "compile-tests": "tsc -p . --outDir out",
    "lint": "eslint src",
    "pretest": "npm run compile-tests && npm run compile && npm run lint",
    "test": "vscode-test",
    "package": "vsce package"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "vscode-languageclient": "^9.0.1"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "@eslint/js": "^9.0.0",
    "@types/mocha": "^10.0.6",
    "@types/node": "^20.11.0",
    "@types/vscode": "^1.85.0",
    "@vscode/test-cli": "^0.0.10",
    "@vscode/test-electron": "^2.4.0",
    "@vscode/vsce": "^3.0.0",
    "esbuild": "^0.21.0",
    "eslint": "^9.0.0",
    "typescript": "^5.4.0",
    "typescript-eslint": "^8.0.0"
  }
}
